:: Mom watching_tv [interaction] {"position":"850,2225","size":"100,100"}
/* Talk scene ("Chat with her", Define Interactions): $mom on the living room couch in front of the TV.
   Variants 1 (cooking show) and 2 (the crime show recap) always; 3 only when $sister is on the couch too.
   4 while she still works for $boss (Stage 0, before False Sympathy: asleep over his mails). 5 after she lost that
   job (Stage 0, after False Sympathy: daytime TV). 6 from Stage 1 on (the office sitcom).
   7 after No stimulus (mom_controlSession), with a small choice (+1 MomLust if I change the channel back).
   8 after her first corruption stage (The Briefing), with a part that changes after A Knock at Night (mom_nightVisit),
   +1 MomLust. 7 and 8 only when $sister is not in the room. */
<<silently>>
<<set _mtSisHere to setup.npcIsAt("sister", $player.location.sysName)>>
<<set _variants to [1, 2]>>
<<if _mtSisHere>><<run _variants.push(3)>><</if>>
<<if $company.stage == 0 && !setup.questDone("mom_falseSympathy")>><<run _variants.push(4)>><</if>>
<<if $company.stage == 0 && setup.questDone("mom_falseSympathy")>><<run _variants.push(5)>><</if>>
<<if $company.stage >= 1>><<run _variants.push(6)>><</if>>
<<if setup.questDone("mom_controlSession") && !_mtSisHere>><<run _variants.push(7)>><</if>>
<<if $mom.corruptionStage >= 1 && !_mtSisHere>><<run _variants.push(8)>><</if>>
<<set _pick to setup.pickTalkScene("Mom watching_tv", _variants)>>
<</silently>>
<<DisplayActivity $mom 500>>
<<switch _pick>>

/* ——— 1: The cooking show ——— */
<<case 1>>
On the TV, a man with a lot of forearm tattoos is making a deconstructed shepherd's pie, and $mom.callName is taking it personally. She's sitting on the very edge of the couch with a bowl of apple slices in her lap, and she hasn't eaten one in a while, because her hands are busy pointing at the screen.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Look at him, honey, look at what he's doing to that poor potato." },
{ who: $player, text: "He's deconstructing it." },
{ who: $mom, text: "He's ruining it, is what he's doing. A shepherd's pie isn't supposed to be deconstructed, the whole point of a pie is that it's all in one place. Sit down, sweetie, you're blocking the judges." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I sit. She hands me the apple bowl without taking her eyes off the screen, and for the next ten minutes I get a running commentary. The tattooed man is too confident. The woman with the bangs is going to burn her sauce because she keeps waving at the camera. The quiet old man in the corner is going to win, because he cleans his station between steps, and people who clean their station between steps are people you can trust.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I bet you the tattoo guy wins." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, you're on. Loser does the dishes tomorrow." },
{ who: $player, text: "Deal." },
{ text: "The judges take a bite of the deconstructed pie. One of them closes his eyes, and $mom.callName grips my arm." },
{ who: $mom, text: "No. No, don't you dare close your eyes, you traitor." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The tattooed man wins. $mom.callName stares at the screen in silence while the confetti comes down, then gets up, takes the apple bowl back out of my hands, and goes to the kitchen to do the dishes tonight, so she won't have to hear about it tomorrow.

/* ——— 2: Previously on ——— */
<<case 2>>
The TV has stopped and is politely asking whether anybody is still watching. $mom.callName is still watching. She's glaring at the screen with the remote in her hand, as if she's been accused of something.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Of course I'm still watching, who else would be watching? It's very judgmental, this thing." },
{ who: $player, text: "How many episodes have you seen today?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "That's none of its business, and it's none of yours either. Sit down, you can catch up, I'll tell you everything." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's some Scandinavian crime show where everyone wears very nice sweaters and nobody ever turns the lights on. She recaps the first five episodes for me in about two minutes, without pausing for breath. There's a detective whose wife left, and a body in a lake, and a second body in a different lake, and a farmer who definitely did it except that he didn't, and the detective's partner, who has a secret, which might be about the lakes or might be about her ex-husband, $mom.callName isn't sure yet.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "So who did it?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "The pastor." },
{ who: $player, text: "There's a pastor?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "He's in one scene, sweetie, in episode two, and he was holding a cup of coffee in a very suspicious way." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She presses play. Six minutes into the episode, the pastor comes back, holding a different cup of coffee, and she grabs my knee and doesn't say anything, she just squeezes, very hard, and doesn't let go until the scene changes.

/* ——— 3: A male opinion (only when $sister is on the couch too) ——— */
<<case 3>>
They've taken one end of the couch each, with a single blanket stretched across the middle, and they're watching a dating show where a dozen men in very tight shirts are trying to impress a woman on a yacht. $sister.callName has her phone out and is keeping some kind of score. $mom.callName has a cushion pressed to her chest and looks like she can't decide whether she disapproves.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Oh, thank god. Sit down, little $sister.callPlayerShort, we need a male opinion, preferably a bad one so we can ignore it." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Be nice to your $sister.playerRelation." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I am being nice. I said 'preferably'." },
{ text: "On the screen, a man named Tanner is showing the woman on the yacht his abs and explaining that he's 'really into honesty'." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So, Tanner. Yes or no?" },
{ who: $player, text: "No way. Anybody who has to tell you he's into honesty is lying about something." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Thank you. He's a seven at best, he has a podcast, and $mom.callName gave him a nine." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I did not give him a nine! I said he had nice teeth, and teeth matter, sweetheart. You'll see when you're older." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I squeeze in between them, which steals most of the blanket, and for the next half hour I'm the deciding vote on everything: whose shirt is worse, who's lying, whether a man who cries at the first sunset is sensitive or a professional. $sister.callName writes my votes down. $mom.callName argues with every single one and then goes along with them anyway.

At the end, the woman on the yacht picks Tanner. $sister.callName throws her phone onto the blanket in disgust. $mom.callName very quietly says 'teeth', to nobody in particular, and looks extremely pleased with herself.

/* ——— 4: Asleep over his mails (Stage 0, she still works for him) ——— */
<<case 4>>
She's fallen asleep sitting up. The TV is murmuring something about mortgage rates, her head has slid sideways onto the armrest, and there's a laptop on her knees that is slowly, very slowly, slipping toward the floor.

I catch it. The screen wakes up under my hand, and it's her work mail, open on a message from $boss.callName sent at 9:47 in the evening. The subject line is in capitals, THIS IS NOT ACCEPTABLE, and the mail itself is two lines long. The second line just says 'Fix it before you come in.' There's no 'please' and no name at the bottom. She was halfway through typing her answer. It starts with 'I'm so sorry' and is already three paragraphs long.

I read his mail twice. The second time I read it slowly, the way you read the small print in a contract, and I look at the time stamp and the list of people he copied in. Then I close the laptop, very gently, so the click won't wake her, and set it on the coffee table.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ text: "When I pull the throw over her, she stirs." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Mm. I'm awake, honey, I'm just resting my eyes." },
{ who: $player, text: "I know you are." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Did I send it? I have to send him that mail before..." },
{ who: $player, text: "You can send it in the morning. Go back to sleep." },
{ who: $mom, text: "In the morning. Okay, sweetie." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She's asleep again before she has finished saying it. I turn the TV down until the man talking about mortgages is just a mumble, and I leave the lamp on, the way she always leaves it on for us.

/* ——— 5: Daytime TV (Stage 0, after False Sympathy) ——— */
<<case 5>>
It's the middle of a weekday, and $mom.callName is on the couch in her robe, watching a talk show. The host is a woman with enormous hair, and today she's giving away cars, or possibly vacuum cleaners. Everybody in the audience is screaming either way. When $mom.callName sees me, she grabs the remote and switches over to the news, much too fast.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "You can switch it back, you know. I won't tell anybody." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Switch what back? I was watching the news, I'm very informed." },
{ text: "On the news, a man is talking about soybean futures. She nods along seriously for about fifteen seconds. Then she sighs and switches back." },
{ who: $mom, text: "The host has a dog called Biscuit, and she brings him on every Wednesday, and I know that, honey. I know what day the dog comes." },
{ who: $player, text: "That's not so bad. Biscuit sounds like a good dog." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I've also watched four episodes of a show about people who buy houses in Portugal, and I don't even want a house in Portugal. I couldn't find it on a map. I know it's next to Spain, but that's as far as I get." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I sit down with her. She tucks her feet under her robe and tells me which of the Portugal couples got divorced afterward, according to the internet, and which ones she thinks will be next. She has strong opinions about all of them.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "When do you think there'll be something for me to do? At the company, I mean. I don't want to rush you, sweetie." },
{ who: $player, text: "Soon, I promise. I've got a couple of things lined up, I just need one of them to actually say yes." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I know you're working on it, and I'm not complaining, honey, I'd just like to have somewhere to be again. I was always somewhere." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

On the screen, the host is crying and hugging a woman who has just won a car, and Biscuit is barking at both of them. $mom.callName laughs, and wipes her eye with the sleeve of her robe, and tells me it's just the hair, the hair always gets to her.

/* ——— 6: The office sitcom (Stage 1) ——— */
<<case 6>>
She's found an old office sitcom, the kind with the shaky camera and people looking straight into it after every bad joke. She's halfway through the second season and has a notepad on the armrest. When I sit down, she taps it with her pen.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I've been casting it with our people, but you can't tell anybody." },
{ who: $player, text: "Oh no. Okay, go on, who's who?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "The one with the tie who keeps finding his stapler in the jelly, that's $ethan.name, obviously." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah, that's fair." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And the quiet one with the beard who fixes the copier and never says anything, that's $brian.name, and the clever one in the nice shirts who's much too good for the place is $darius.name." },
{ who: $player, text: "So who am I? Please don't say the boss." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

On the screen, the boss is standing in the middle of the office giving a speech that nobody wants to hear, and doing an accent. $mom.callName looks at him, and then at me, and I watch her decide.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Nobody. There isn't anybody for you on this show, honey. The boss on this show is a nice man who doesn't know what he's doing." },
{ who: $player, text: "So I'm not nice?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "You know what you're doing, sweetie, that's not the same thing at all." },
{ text: "She says it lightly, and writes something on the notepad, and turns it face down on the armrest before I can see it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

We watch two more episodes. Every time somebody on the show does something stupid, she says the name of one of my employees under her breath, and every time she's right.

/* ——— 7: The blender (after No stimulus, small choice) ——— */
<<case 7>>
It's some romantic drama with a lot of rain in it. When I sit down next to her, the old cushion sags and tips her half an inch toward me, and she rearranges the throw over her knees until there's a neat fold of blanket between us.

On the screen, the rain has driven the couple into a barn. The music swells. He pushes the wet hair off her face, she pulls his shirt up over his head, he starts on the buttons of her dress, and $mom.callName finds the remote faster than I've ever seen her find anything.

The channel changes. A very cheerful man is now crushing ice in a blender.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, look, a blender." },
{ who: $player, text: "We have a blender." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Not like this one, sweetie, look at that, it does soup." },
{ text: "She watches the blender do soup with tremendous concentration. Her cheeks are red, and the remote is still in her hand, pointed at the TV, with her thumb resting on the channel button just in case." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<div id="mom-tv-blender">
<<link "Change it back">><<replace "#mom-tv-blender">>
I hold out my hand for the remote. She looks at it. She looks at the blender man, who is now making frozen yogurt, and then she gives me the remote, because I'm holding out my hand, and that's still enough.

I switch back to the barn. They've made good progress without us. $mom.callName sits completely still with the throw clutched in her lap, looking very hard at the lamp next to the TV, as if the lamp has started doing something interesting.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "We could watch something else, honey. There's a documentary about bees on, I think, or there was earlier." },
{ who: $player, text: "No, leave it. I want to see how it ends." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh. Okay, then." },
{ text: "She doesn't get up. After a while, her eyes slide back to the screen, and they stay there. I don't look at her, and she doesn't look at me, and when the scene finally ends with the two of them asleep in the hay, she reaches for her tea, which went cold an hour ago, and drinks the whole mug without stopping." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomLust" 1>>
<</replace>><</link>>
<<link "Let her have the blender">><<replace "#mom-tv-blender">>
I leave her the blender. We watch the cheerful man make soup, smoothies, almond butter and, for some reason, cookie dough, and by the end of it $mom.callName has gone from pretending to be interested to actually being interested.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "It's only eighty-nine dollars, honey, in three easy payments." },
{ who: $player, text: "We still have a blender." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Our blender can't do almond butter. Our blender can barely do a banana." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She has her phone out before the ad is over. I talk her out of it, which takes two minutes and a promise to look at the reviews tomorrow. She's much calmer now. She's still sitting with the fold of blanket between us, though, and she doesn't move it.
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>

/* ——— 8: Not tonight (after The Briefing, part changes after A Knock at Night) ——— */
<<case 8>>
<<if setup.questDone("mom_nightVisit")>>
She's in her robe, with her hair still damp from the shower, a mug of tea on the coffee table and her feet up on the couch. When she sees me, she pulls her feet in to make room for me, and then, after a moment, she stretches them back out across my lap. She doesn't say anything about it.

The show is something about antiques. A man with a magnifying glass is explaining to a woman that her vase is worth less than she thought. At the first commercial, $mom.callName mutes it, and the living room goes very quiet.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Is it bad tonight?" },
{ text: "She asks the muted TV, very softly and very matter-of-fact, the way she used to ask whether I had homework." },
{ who: $player, text: "No, not tonight. I'm okay." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Good. I'm glad, sweetie." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She nods and unmutes the TV. Her feet stay in my lap. She doesn't like antiques shows, she's told me so a dozen times, but she watches this one all the way to the end anyway, and the next one after that, and she doesn't go up to bed until I do.
<<else>>
She's sitting at the far end of the couch with her knees drawn up and a cooking magazine she isn't reading. When I sit down in the middle, she doesn't move away. She doesn't move at all.

The show is something about antiques. A man with a magnifying glass is explaining to a woman that her vase is worth less than she thought.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, about that morning..." },
{ who: $player, text: "What about it?" },
{ text: "She opens her mouth, and closes it, and turns a page of the magazine she isn't reading." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Nothing, sweetie, it's nothing. Did you eat? There's soup in the fridge." },
{ who: $player, text: "I ate at the office, thanks." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, good. That's good." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She turns the volume up two notches, and then one more. We watch the man with the magnifying glass break the news to three more people. Once, during the third one, she glances sideways at my hands, resting on my knees, and then back at the screen so quickly that the magazine slides off her lap. She lets it lie on the floor.
<</if>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomLust" 1>>

<</switch>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 1>>

<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Leave her to her show" $player.location.passage>><</link>></div>
